__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Finder writes one of these into every folder it has ever displayed.
# Nine were tracked, including one at the repo root, so they arrived in
# the deploy and turned up in every `git status` after browsing the
# project. The pattern is unanchored on purpose: it has to catch a
# nested one as well as the root.
.DS_Store

# The cache travels as data_cache.zip, not as 148,684 loose files.
# Tracking them made Streamlit Cloud's checkout unreliable -- twice it
# deployed a new app.py beside a stale engine/ -- so the folder is a
# local working directory now and tools/pack_cache.py builds the
# archive that gets committed. engine/cache_archive.py has the whole
# reasoning. To get the folder back on a fresh clone:
#     python3 tools/pack_cache.py --unpack
data_cache/
data_cache.zip.tmp
logs/

# Local prediction tracker file (production uses Postgres; see engine/log_store.py)
prediction_log.csv
prediction_log.csv.lock
prediction_log.csv.tmp.*

# Regenerated by build_backtest_population.py in a couple of minutes from
# data_cache/; 65 MB of derived rows that would otherwise be cloned on
# every Streamlit Cloud deploy.
backtest_population.csv
backtest_player_games.csv

# Raw odds API responses. Captured nightly and kept LOCALLY ONLY:
# SportsGameOdds' terms forbid redistributing their data through
# "downloadable files, bulk exports" and this repo is public, so the
# raw responses must never be committed. What travels instead is
# line_records/ -- our own projections, the outcome, and a SHA-256 of
# each raw response, so a claim can be audited against a file that is
# produced on request rather than republished.
line_snapshots/
